==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|insouciance}}, from {{m|fr|in-||not}} + {{m|fr|souciant||worrying}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈsuːsi.əns/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-insouciance.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[carelessness|Carelessness]], [[heedlessness]], [[indifference]], or [[casual]] [[unconcern]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Steven Levy|title=The Unabomber and David Gelernter|work=The New York Times|date=1995-05-21|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1995/05/21/magazine/the-unabomber-and-david-gelertner.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=So Gelernter, with an '''insouciance''' he now regrets, also chose a Lovelace as a namesake—Linda, the lead actress in "Deep Throat."}}
# [[nonchalance|Nonchalance]].
#* '''2024,''' Patrik Jonsson and Melanie Stetson Freeman, ''[https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Society/2024/0827/free-state-of-Florida-liberty-wildness Florida woman kills wild boar with mango. (This is not a meme.)],'' in: The Christian Science Monitor, August 27 2024
#*: She almost felt insulted by [the wild boar's] '''insouciance''' as it rooted in her grove.

